  "published": "2026-11-11T09:04:54.617Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Default ZIP compression is now zlib level 3 for both XLSX and XLSB through a built-in ZIP writer, making writes 13-21% faster at a slightly larger file size; pass an explicit CompressionLevel to keep the previous enum-based behaviour. XLSB adds useSharedStrings: false for inline strings, row writes are buffered, shared strings are encoded in bulk, and ExcelReaderAbstract.CurrentRow exposes the current row as ReadOnlySpan<FieldInfo> without boxing. XLSX reads now use byte scanners for worksheets and shared strings, preserving rich text, entities, xml:space and _xHHHH_ escapes while falling back to XmlReader for unsupported markup; worksheet UTF-8 is validated incrementally, and the 1904 date system is honored for both XLSX and XLSB. Readers now open files read-only with FileShare.Read, so read-only files and concurrent readers work.",
